:[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T18:14:37-08:00","id":1467957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1467955#post1467955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, typo.<br /> <br /> My bad.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's fine, it happens. I'd appreciate that being edited for clarity though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T18:28:45-08:00","id":1467959,"title":"","content":"Anywayyyy...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1467950#post1467950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the SI is going to be portrayed a number of ways, not the least being that they are going to be every bit as corrupt, cruel, inefficient, and alternatively genius versus incompetent. For example, I have no difficulty believing the Second Inquisition can and will conduct all manner of anti-terrorist operations throughout the world as well as military activities that should blow the Masquerade wide open.<br /> <br /> We've seen Operation: Antigen in London, the massive &quot;gang war&quot; that happened in LA by Night, the military operations that attacked the largest building in Vienna (in the Mausoleum), and undoubtedly many other acts of kidnapping, torture, and mass murder.<br /> <br /> I also believe the Second Inquisition will get away with these with almost no oversight because the World of Darkness is full of corrupt, lazy, ignorant, and uniformed masses who are utterly uninterested in the truth. That is the basis of the game that the supernatural is real and no one believes in it because they prefer to wallow in their own ignorance. It is not the REAL world and the fact people expect it to be is something I feel that's a mistake.<br /> <br /> I also fully expect that the Second Inquisition will have members who want to commit genocide, members who don't want to commit the necessary resources to destroy all vampires, members who just want to monitor the situation, members who want to use the Kindred, and those who would LOVE to commit genocide but are of the mind that it would be too expensive/require too many resources.<br /> <br /> I expect them to be ignorant Right Wing paranoics who are convinced of their own righteousness but vicious as well as incompetant in other ways. I expect large amounts of casualties and people attacking vampires at night along with perfectly planned operations in equal measure. The Second Inquisition should be like the War on Drugs and War on Terror.<br /> <br /> Tens of thousands of casualties but the vampires never go extinct and even thrive eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's basically a tautology to say it makes sense because it happened though, which is what this argument boils down to when saying &quot;these things happened and they went fine too&quot;, that doesn't make them make sense, it just makes the writing stand out as demanding that they do.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;it makes sense because it's the World of Darkness&quot; past a certain point verges on being the sidebar in Ravenloft 5e that says &quot;nothing about how the domains work have to make sense because the Dark Powers are making it work.&quot; That works for Ravenloft because there are actual nigh omnipotent magical gods regularly actively warping all reality to make it work like how would amuse them. Even at the most generous reading of Mage, to go there for a minute, that's not how the WoD has worked (and also we're talking about Vampire 5th anyway). Verisimilitude, especially in a setting that is supposed to at least use the modern day as its launching point, is a thing. The magical bits are supposed to lurk beneath the surface of an at least roughly recognizable world. Expecting it thus to function in some way like that one should is a consequence of making that narrative move. If anything, the world being ours, but worse, would make extreme reactions more likely, not less likely. Otherwise at some point it's all just a convenient narrative dodge for having to reconcile events with logic. It's the wanting it both ways problem. Okay, the world is at least supposed to resemble ours, but in that case things are going to resemble the way people and organizations react within it. Wait no, the world isn't supposed to resemble ours, people are in fact so lazy and uncaring that these are barely issues. You can't really jam those things together.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if it is the case that people are that corrupt, cruel, inefficient and incompetent, the Second Inquisition should never have been able to rise to the prominence that it did, vampires should have kept being able to manipulate people just fine, because people are that worthless and people prefer to wallow in their own ignorance. These statements and the Second Inquisition rising to happen don't reconcile with each other. They should have never been as effective as they have been in the first place. Certainly not to the point where we can argue about how feasible drone striking Vienna was. <br /> <br /> Alternatively we're right back to &quot;why are vampires still alive&quot;, because according to earlier posts in this thread, the book says that the SI is afraid of publicly exposing their works. But if people work like you say they do in the WoD, then that's not a real problem, and they should be able to finish wiping out vampires unimpeded. <br /> <br /> Basically all these arguments keep feeling like they continue to fold in on and contradict each other, even just for being put forward. <br /> <br /> I feel like I need to reassure people that acknowledging that some of the stuff in 5e is contradictory and dubiously thought out for its implications will not actually make Paradox go &quot;oh crap! they got us!&quot; and make them stop publishing VtM 5th. 5th edition is here to stay, I assure you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T18:34:30-08:00","id":1467960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1467959#post1467959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anywayyyy...<br /> <br /> It's basically a tautology to say it makes sense because it happened though, which is what this argument boils down to when saying &quot;these things happened and they went fine too&quot;, that doesn't make them make sense, it just makes the writing stand out as demanding that they do.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;it makes sense because it's the World of Darkness&quot; past a certain point verges on being the sidebar in Ravenloft 5e that says &quot;nothing about how the domains work have to make sense because the Dark Powers are making it work.&quot; That works for Ravenloft because there are actual nigh omnipotent magical gods regularly actively warping all reality to make it work like how would amuse them. Even at the most generous reading of Mage, to go there for a minute, that's not how the WoD has worked (and also we're talking about Vampire 5th anyway). Verisimilitude, especially in a setting that is supposed to at least use the modern day as its launching point, is a thing. The magical bits are supposed to lurk beneath the surface of an at least roughly recognizable world. Expecting it thus to function in some way like that one should is a consequence of making that narrative move. If anything, the world being ours, but worse, would make extreme reactions more likely, not less likely. Otherwise at some point it's all just a convenient narrative dodge for having to reconcile events with logic. It's the wanting it both ways problem. Okay, the world is at least supposed to resemble ours, but in that case things are going to resemble the way people and organizations react within it. Wait no, the world isn't supposed to resemble ours, people are in fact so lazy and uncaring that these are barely issues. You can't really jam those things together.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if it is the case that people are that corrupt, cruel, inefficient and incompetent, the Second Inquisition should never have been able to rise to the prominence that it did, vampires should have kept being able to manipulate people just fine, because people are that worthless and people prefer to wallow in their own ignorance. These statements and the Second Inquisition rising to happen don't reconcile with each other. They should have never been as effective as they have been in the first place. Certainly not to the point where we can argue about how feasible drone striking Vienna was.<br /> <br /> Alternatively we're right back to &quot;why are vampires still alive&quot;, because according to earlier posts in this thread, the book says that the SI is afraid of publicly exposing their works. But if people work like you say they do in the WoD, then that's not a real problem, and they should be able to finish wiping out vampires unimpeded.<br /> <br /> Basically all these arguments keep feeling like they continue to fold in on and contradict each other, even just for being put forward.<br /> <br /> I feel like I need to reassure people that acknowledging that some of the stuff in 5e is contradictory and dubiously thought out for its implications will not actually make Paradox go &quot;oh crap! they got us!&quot; and make them stop publishing VtM 5th. 5th edition is here to stay, I assure you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused at the idea that governments that are corrupt, cruel, inefficient, and incompetent are somehow unbelievable at rising to power. I find the idea of them being hyper-efficient and morally pure to be something that would dramatically impede their rise to power. The Second Inquisition being a representation of authoritarianism and unchecked government power (remember, its a Gothic PUNK) game means that they would almost certainly represent the absolute worse abuses of government power.<br /> <br /> But I suppose I feel like the War on Terror IS the inspiration for the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> It's meant to represent an erosion of civil liberites, paranoia, and the sense of being hunted as well as persecuted by the government.<br /> <br /> I think the attempt to link Al-Qaeda, anti-terrorism, and drone strikes in the Vienna attack was less meant to be a literal representation of how the Inquisition would work but to create a direct link between the War on Terror and the persecution of Kindred in the minds of the reader.<br /> <br /> Why &quot;The Sabbat claim credit for 9/11&quot; is front and center even though its both offensive AND stupid.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T18:47:32-08:00","id":1467965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1467960#post1467960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm confused at the idea that governments that are corrupt, cruel, inefficient, and incompetent are somehow unbelievable at rising to power. I find the idea of them being hyper-efficient and morally pure to be something that would dramatically impede their rise to power. The Second Inquisition being a representation of authoritarianism and unchecked government power (remember, its a Gothic PUNK) game means that they would almost certainly represent the absolute worse abuses of government power.<br /> <br /> But I suppose I feel like the War on Terror IS the inspiration for the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> It's meant to represent an erosion of civil liberites, paranoia, and the sense of being hunted as well as persecuted by the government.<br /> <br /> I think the attempt to link Al-Qaeda, anti-terrorism, and drone strikes in the Vienna attack was less meant to be a literal representation of how the Inquisition would work but to create a direct link between the War on Terror and the persecution of Kindred in the minds of the reader.<br /> <br /> Why &quot;The Sabbat claim credit for 9/11&quot; is front and center even though its both offensive AND stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can think it wasn't meant to be literal, but the writing presents it as a literal thing that happened, which means it's sitting there, having happened, to be reconciled with for its implications. You want governments to be cruel, corrupt and inefficient. You also want them to be so effective and efficient they can do something like drone strike Vienna and completely cover it up with no problems. It was a literal representation of the Inquisition at work. That's just.. the material.<br /> <br /> Presenting two ideas that don't go together and trying to move out of that with &quot;well it's a metaphor&quot; really doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Especially when it makes your argument selective to a point of being arbitrary. If people are that corrupt and worthless, vampires should have been able to manipulate the Second Inquisition away from ever being a problem. They don't want to know what's going on in the world anyway, by your note.<br /> <br /> When Lucifer sings &quot;Crime solving Devil, it makes sense, don't overthink it.&quot; in the show Lucifer, it's funny because it's self referential humour.<br /> <br /> When you're going &quot;The Vienna chantry got blown up by drone strikes by an international military/governmental/intelligence agency alliance that then totally covers it up, but vampires are generally still alive, it makes sense, don't overthink it.&quot; it's... something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-15-2021, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T03:10:05-08:00","id":1467981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1467950#post1467950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not the REAL world and the fact people expect it to be is something I feel that's a mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not the real world and no one expects it to be, this is not the argument.<br /> <br /> Fiction relies on Suspension of Disbelief, but not every reader have the same bar for it, and indeed not everyone take the same elements at the same value. Too stretched it rips, and you lose some readers. That's the whole reason we have discussions about what's believable here.<br /> <br /> This <b>is</b> above metaphor, tropes and everything else. You have to convince the reader that the artistic value of the work is worth Suspension, not to demand the reader to Suspend so they may see the Art. It is always first and foremost on the author, not the reader.<br /> <br /> So let me talk about me, about my Suspension of Disbelief. self-consistency is <u><i><b>extremely</b></i></u> important to me. And in this, <b><i>commitment to a conclusion</i></b>. Since my childhood I always hated deeply those episodes in shows where a major development happens just to be scratched in name of the <i>status quo</i>. The hero reveals their secret identity to someone, then a silly happenstance convince the person that it was a mistake or this memory is erased? Please, erase this crap from <b>my</b> memory, watching it was the only mistake.<br /> <br /> You say the SI will be portrayed a number of ways. What does it mean? Are they so subtle that their actions and methods can't be confirmed? Are they so fragmented that different sections do different things? Are they powerful enough to force their way? Or are they just going to pull out all sorts of shenanigans and nothing happens because the <i>status quo</i> has plot armor?<br /> <br /> Each of those options is valid, but each have its own consequences. If you just ignore logical consequences your reasons don't matter to me anymore. If you go for the last option it won't work for me anyway. I don't care how close WoD is to RL, I don't care if the <i>status quo</i>is maintained or not, I <b>do </b>expect commitment to a course of action and self-consistency.<br /> <br /> About the metaphor itself, both the War on Terror and the War on Drugs are full of unintended consequences all over the place. Scores of people that do not buy and never bought the official narrative, and not only people marked as conspiracy theorists. Indeed, sometimes the official narrative was itself denounced as baseless conspiracy theory, without prejudice to it being still the official narrative. And now, in the world post-wikileaks and 4chan, where anyone can generate lasting evidence with their phones, it's even harder to believe anyone have this level of control over the narrative.<br /> <br /> Let me repeat, my thing is to explore consequences. Can they pressure the official narrative to be such and such and authorities be completely unable to stop them? Of course they can. When I was born my country was still under a US-backed military dictatorship whose narratives are twisted and covered to this day and only recently we obtained enough evidence to justly call Bull Shit on it. Yet, while a lot of people bought the official narrative completely, enough people refused and dived deeper to form resistance groups, warfare and whatnot. The cover-up being effective never stopped the truth of having consequences, and I don't need an Italian to tell me how cover-ups work. My father was a resistance member at the time and personally knew a number of people whose disappearances are unexplained still. The conflict between narratives then still shapes Brazil's political landscape.<br /> <br /> When the Second Inquisition is high-profile enough to carry out drone strikes in the middle of Europe, but too low profile to turn the setting into a survival horror landscape for vampires, widespread enough to control the narratives in every country in the world, but narrow enough to not have whistle blowers, coordinated enough to stop any third party from messing up the scheme, but not enough to stop its members from engaging in fragmented action, people caring enough for the SI to exist, but then being completely indifferent to any terrorist action, there are just too many inconsistencies for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T04:20:49-08:00","id":1467984,"title":"","content":"I think that this is a good point. When you have an organisation that is purposefully written vague to fit into different narratives, there still has to be an underlying logic and consistancy to it (if you want to make your world believable). The connections between intelligence services and the Vampire society as it is written right now doesn't make much sense. This doesn't matter much if you want to have them as a boogie man or antagonist in your campaign, but it definitly hurts the overall story of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27028,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","user":"Ignithas","date":". 11-16-2021, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T05:07:20-08:00","id":1467990,"title":"","content":"For me, I find myself going back to the fact that this is the same setting in which a bunch of robot-wizards blew up an ancient vampire using laserbeams from outer-space and then rewrote reality so that everyone believed that it was all just a natural typhoon disaster. And if something like that can happen in the setting, then a big bomb getting dropped on a building in Europe and having it get passed off as a terrorist attack doesn't overly break the verisimilitude for me.<br /> <br /> Of course, my assumption is that the SI has supernatural backing of some sort, so it's more easy to write off inconsistencies as &quot;it's magic, I don't have to explain it.&quot; Though it helps that the SI hasn't been explored at all. If it turns out that it's all just mundane humans then the inconsistences can't really be written away and we're stuck with the inconsistencies ripping the setting to pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T06:29:19-08:00","id":1467996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1467990#post1467990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, I find myself going back to the fact that this is the same setting in which a bunch of robot-wizards blew up an ancient vampire using laserbeams from outer-space and then rewrote reality so that everyone believed that it was all just a natural typhoon disaster. And if something like that can happen in the setting, then a big bomb getting dropped on a building in Europe and having it get passed off as a terrorist attack doesn't overly break the verisimilitude for me.<br /> <br /> Of course, my assumption is that the SI has supernatural backing of some sort, so it's more easy to write off inconsistencies as &amp;quot;it's magic, I don't have to explain it.&amp;quot; Though it helps that the SI hasn't been explored at all. If it turns out that it's all just mundane humans then the inconsistences can't really be written away and we're stuck with the inconsistencies ripping the setting to pieces.</div> </div> </div> </div>This! I really feel like the Vienna bombing is just another Tuesday to most people in the setting. As soon as you have secret societies all sense of realism goes out of the window. <br /> <br /> Where the story doesn't work for you, are you able to use those contradictions to add game? How high up does the conspiracy go is a classic part of this genre, and VtM. Would an operation of that scale require supernatural cover up? Great, who did it? <br /> Is Europe now trying to go to war with some not clearly defined enemy again? How is that affecting local politics? <br /> I'm half way through plotting an intro game at the moment where the PCs are tasked with dealing with some conspiracy theorists looking into the attacks, only to find an SI cell doing the same thing.<br /> <br /> Of all the things in the setting that don't make sense why does this one feel so important to people?<br /> <br /> P.S. I hope the inquisition aren't made out to be totally Evil and there remain some members who are trying to save the world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25078-brickman","name":"Brickman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T07:05:33-08:00","id":1467998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of all the things in the setting that don't make sense why does this one feel so important to people? </div> </div> </div>Amongst other things, because a solid, let's say half of the praise people keep giving to V5 is how it's all so much more grounded compared to previous editions of vampire, but when the need to defend something like the Vienna drone strike as sensible writing comes up, that suddenly goes out the window to say &quot;well things shouldn't be expected to make sense&quot; or &quot;well that was a metaphor&quot;, or &quot;mortals would ignore it because they're corrupt, incompetent and lazy and want to ignore the supernatural world, but also somehow despite all those things being true, mortals still cared enough about noticing the supernatural to facilitate the rise of the Second Inquisition, which was so competent it could do things like make drone strikes happen in a major European city and then cover it up with no problems.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's pretty glaring as far as jangly, even arbitrary contradictions when on the one hand the WoD is supposed to be a setting that uses the modern world as a baseline to roll from, but on the other hand, no, no, disregard what something of that caliber would mean if it happened in the modern world, people in the WoD don't in fact behave in ways even remotely close to people. And the best that can be offered seems to just be &quot;it doesn't have to make sense anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's otherwise glaring for the sheer power an organization would have to have to both enact and then cover up something like drone striking Vienna, that said organizations focus is wiping out vampires, but there are still vampires. No one is saying &quot;secret societies don't exist and don't cover things up in the WoD&quot;, what some people are saying is &quot;for a secret society to get away with both enacting this particular event and covering it up, would make them have to be so powerful that the continued existence of their enemies in the state that they currently exist makes no sense.&quot;<br /> <br /> And it really doesn't help when all the current attempt to explain that away boils down to &quot;make up your own answer, it's not the job of the setting to have to make sense.&quot; If I pay a not small amount of money for these books and the setting they create, I don't think it's a lot to ask for some basic internal consistency and narrative rigor with such that they create.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-16-2021, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T07:36:13-08:00","id":1468001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1467998#post1467998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Amongst other things, because a solid, let's say half of the praise people keep giving to V5 is how it's all so much more grounded compared to previous editions of vampire, but when the need to defend something like the Vienna drone strike as sensible writing comes up, that suddenly goes out the window to say &quot;well things shouldn't be expected to make sense&quot; or &quot;well that was a metaphor&quot;, or &quot;mortals would ignore it because they're corrupt, incompetent and lazy and want to ignore the supernatural world, but also somehow despite all those things being true, mortals still cared enough about noticing the supernatural to facilitate the rise of the Second Inquisition, which was so competent it could do things like make drone strikes happen in a major European city and then cover it up with no problems.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can just say me.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition is something that is, in canon, established as something that is very good at fighting vampires in some situations but also complete failures in other places. They are not something that has managed to destroy Kindred society but they have managed to inflict significant damage on vampiredom. They are not going to exterminate vampiredom but they might be able to decimate its ranks. The Second Inquisition is something that is meant to be a THREAT to vampire society but the game is not and has never portrayed the SI as something that will destroy all vampires or even get rid of the major sects.<br /> <br /> Not in its current form as is.<br /> <br /> This is a feature not a bug and every supplement has highlighted Kindred society getting along with the business of Elysium, sect wars, controlling the masses behind the scenes, and feeding at the Succubus Club. The biggest successes of the SI like the Cleansing of London and the Vienna chantry were possibly also inside jobs (which is something I hate conspiracy theory wise but whatcha gonna do). The developers DO NOT WANT the SI to be an existential threat to Kindred everywhere. It wants to use the SI to drive them deeper into the shadows and also shake up the previous status quo.<br /> <br /> I think part of the issue is that a lot of people keep trying to make this a monolithic organization when it is explictly not. There are going to be individual members like Sullivan Dane and Felicity Price (who is a NWO asset in the SAD) who are the greatest vampire hunters ever. They are well-informed, cautious, and skilled. This is a contrast to the Mortician's Army in Winter's Teeth, who are sucking MORONS and get themselves all killed attacking a Justicar at night. Both are products of the fact that social media and changing times mean vampires are more exposed than ever.<br /> <br /> It also is not in any way shape or form WEIRD to state the SI has a lot of power, reach, and influence but also cannot root out a race of supernatural individuals with that. When I say its a metaphor for the War on Terror, I am not saying, &quot;So it doesn't make sense&quot;, I am illustrating that the governments of the world cannot root out terrorists across the globe completely no matter how much money and force they throw at it.<br /> <br /> The same for vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-16-2021, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T07:54:47-08:00","id":1468003,"title":"","content":"Saying that contradictory writing is a feature and not a bug is the exact problem people are having when they note how badly this sustains the idea of suspension of disbelief. The concept that &quot;well when I need them to be absolutely hypercompetent, they are absolutely hypercompetent, but when I need them to be incompetent failures, they are incompetent failures&quot; isn't clever or adaptive writing, it's arbitrary writing that treats stuff like simple narrative logic with what then comes off as straight up disdain.<br /> <br /> The WoD at least likes to pretend it is presenting a coherent setting with a coherent narrative. Not &quot;this is all an existential metaphor anyway, so the actual details are meaningless.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a feature not a bug and every supplement has highlighted Kindred society getting along with the business of Elysium, sect wars, controlling the masses behind the scenes, and feeding at the Succubus Club. The biggest successes of the SI like the Cleansing of London and the Vienna chantry were possibly also inside jobs (which is something I hate conspiracy theory wise but whatcha gonna do). The developers DO NOT WANT the SI to be an existential threat to Kindred everywhere. It wants to use the SI to drive them deeper into the shadows and also shake up the previous status quo. </div> </div> </div>Good for the developers. Maybe they should have thought about that before giving the SI capacity that would make them an existential threat to kindred everywhere. Saying what the writers want only makes it more glaring when their own writing flies in the face of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think part of the issue is that a lot of people keep trying to make this a monolithic organization when it is explictly not. </div> </div> </div>No, part of the issue is giving the SI accomplishments that would only be possible or make sense for a vastly powerful, monolithic organization, then when someone points that out, getting a reply of &quot;nuh uh&quot;.<br /> <br /> You seem to feel that when part of the entire problem with something like the Vienna incident is how contradictory it is to this stuff you talk about as far as intent and the like, that pointing out the things it contradicts somehow makes it not contradict them. That's not how anything works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also is not in any way shape or form WEIRD to state the SI has a lot of power, reach, and influence but also cannot root out a race of supernatural individuals with that. </div> </div> </div>Allcaps and insisting that what you say makes sense, does not actually make it make sense. It is in fact super weird that the SI can enact a military drone strike into a major European city, then cover it up with no problems or consequences for reasons at this point outlined by several posters at length across multiple posts, but somehow cannot root out a race of vampires with the level of global reach and influence they would have had to do that. It ignores logic, scale, consequences, narrative logic..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I say its a metaphor for the War on Terror, I am not saying, &quot;So it doesn't make sense&quot;, I am illustrating that the governments of the world cannot root out terrorists across the globe completely no matter how much money and force they throw at it. </div> </div> </div>The governments of the world (certainly the Western chunk of it) do not particularly work with what would need to a level of sheer international coordination, influence and unity of purpose that they could enact a military drone strike in a major European city and then cover it up with no issues or consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am illustrating that the governments of the world cannot root out terrorists across the globe completely no matter how much money and force they throw at it. </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are illustrating it by making an analogy that falls apart when comparing it to the actual writing used in game to try and make that analogy. I'm sure the developers totally have in mind the things you say they have in mind. That doesn't change that when it came time for the execution of they had in mind, what the result became is a jangling, contradictory mess where the SI veers from all powerful to not, without rhyme or reason, nor basic consideration of the ramifications of the events they ascribe to it. Saying &quot;War on Terror analogy&quot; over and over doesn't change that. It's not a get out of narrative logic free mantra.<br /> <br /> Again: Exclaiming that such is not how the SI works again and again only makes it that much more noticeable that a piece of writing thereby completely ignores such things as far as how you want it to work/note how the developers want it to work. That's part of the point when people go &quot;the Vienna incident is bad writing&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-16-2021, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T08:05:14-08:00","id":1468006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468003#post1468003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying that contradictory writing is a feature and not a bug is the exact problem people are having when they note how badly this sustains the idea of suspension of disbelief. The concept that &quot;well when I need them to be absolutely hypercompetent, they are absolutely hypercompetent, but when I need them to be incompetent failures, they are incompetent failures&quot; isn't clever or adaptive writing, it's arbitrary writing that treats stuff like simple narrative logic with what then comes off as straight up disdain.<br /> <br /> The WoD at least likes to pretend it is presenting a coherent setting with a coherent narrative. Not &quot;this is all an existential metaphor anyway, so the actual details are meaningless.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we fundamentally have very different perceptions about how government, conspiracies, and the SI SHOULD be presented.<br /> <br /> I see them as a coalition of amateurs and professionals working together with some very good and some very bad as well as a lot of mistaken assumptions fumbling around in the dark but a lot of resources as well as influence.<br /> <br /> How do you think they should be portrayed?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T08:24:57-08:00","id":1468007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468006#post1468006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we fundamentally have very different perceptions about how government, conspiracies, and the SI SHOULD be presented.<br /> <br /> I see them as a coalition of amateurs and professionals working together with some very good and some very bad as well as a lot of mistaken assumptions fumbling around in the dark but a lot of resources as well as influence.<br /> <br /> How do you think they should be portrayed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The way you see them completely contradicts what they did in Vienna, yet at the same time you do not want to acknowledge this. That isn't an issue of perception on how governments work, that is an issue of, an incident happened in the writing that would require a near ludicrously powerful and influential group with global scale competence to pull off, and you want to ignore that by talking about the very things that the incident contradicts. You are in many ways doing the work of pointing out my problem for me by going on like this. &quot;A collection of amateurs and professionals working together with some good and bad and mistaken assumptions and fumbling around in the dark but a lot of resources and influence&quot; should not be capable of pulling off a military drone strike action in a major European city, then basically perfectly covering it up without consequence or ramification. You'd think you, of all people thus, for wanting the setting and SI to be a particular way, would be the first person to acknowledge when there is writing that glaringly contradicts that as far as calling something poorly written, but in some seeming need to not want to acknowledge something in V5 as poorly written, we're deep into the weeds of this mess instead.<br /> <br /> I'm going to try and be clear about something. When I call the Vienna incident bad writing, that doesn't mean I want it to have happened, nor does it mean that I think it made sense that it happened, and I've pretty clearly said both those things. That means I think that it is bad writing in part because of what should be the logical consequences of it having happened, in any direction, that heavily contradict huge chunks of the existing setting and how it is depicted.<br /> <br /> You are trying to reframe what I am saying into something that it is not.<br /> <br /> There's been a long march to get away from a central point that remains this: If the SI is supposed to be everything you say it is. If the SI is not supposed to be an existential threat to vampires. If the SI is supposed to be this particular metaphor and analogy. Then the whole thing in Vienna is bad writing that contradicts all of that, because it would instead, by logic, make the SI be so vastly powerful and influential that the things you want to be possible, would not be possible without huge nonsensical contradictions in the setting.<br /> <br /> I don't want a hypercompetent/hyperpowerful SI. But Vienna? Only makes sense with a hypercompetent SI. But then the setting, doesn't want a hypercompetent SI. Do you see the problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-16-2021, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T09:08:51-08:00","id":1468010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1467981#post1467981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Second Inquisition is high-profile enough to carry out drone strikes in the middle of Europe, but too low profile to turn the setting into a survival horror landscape for vampires, widespread enough to control the narratives in every country in the world, but narrow enough to not have whistle blowers, coordinated enough to stop any third party from messing up the scheme, but not enough to stop its members from engaging in fragmented action, people caring enough for the SI to exist, but then being completely indifferent to any terrorist action, there are just too many inconsistencies for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">For me, I find myself going back to the fact that this is the same setting in which a bunch of robot-wizards blew up an ancient vampire using laserbeams from outer-space and then rewrote reality so that everyone believed that it was all just a natural typhoon disaster. And if something like that can happen in the setting, then a big bomb getting dropped on a building in Europe and having it get passed off as a terrorist attack doesn't overly break the verisimilitude for me.<br /> <br /> Of course, my assumption is that the SI has supernatural backing of some sort, so it's more easy to write off inconsistencies as &quot;it's magic, I don't have to explain it.<b>&quot;</b> Though it helps that the SI hasn't been explored at all. If it turns out that it's all just mundane humans then the inconsistences can't really be written away and we're stuck with the inconsistencies ripping the setting to pieces.</span></span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A Wizard Did It&quot; It's an ever-useful explanation, yes. I think even then it's useful to question the limits and characteristics of this power to use the trope in an elegant fashion. I.E: A very very common criticism it's to ask why this power isn't used more, if it's seemingly unlimited and so convinient<br /> <br /> As I see it, the Technocracy played all it's cards of &quot;the most powerful mage faction of the world&quot;. Almost literaly: They commited all the resources they had to the task (Code Ragnarok) - and they did this just before third edition. In 3e they've been nerfed thanks to the Avatar Storm. I'm pretty sure this was used to make a point that they can't do *that* every time something awakens.<br /> <br /> Note that in spite of the limitations mages have (like Paradox, and then 3rd edition happened), and in spite of all the very reasonable reasons that were given to the contrary in the &quot;bible&quot;, a lot of people still believes it makes no sense for vampires to be so powerful in a world where the Technocracy exists. H<i>eck; for some the</i> SI <i>makes sense</i> a<i>s the Technocracy *finaly doing something about vampires*</i> - I think all of this says something about the implications of having wizards doing things<br /> <br /> Similarly I would ask: How supernaturaly powerful it's the SI?, are there conditions/limits to that power? . Some want to see the SI as a &quot;badass normal&quot; faction to represent &quot;humanity&quot;. To make some of their most incredible feats involving a &quot;3rd party&quot; <i>could</i> be a good compromise between the tropes. That opens some ways to control the mojo, too, as the 3rd party may not be easily accessible - if at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-16-2021, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T09:43:25-08:00","id":1468015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brickman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1467996#post1467996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of all the things in the setting that don't make sense why does this one feel so important to people?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. This isn't the first and won't be the last thread about something that's too glaringly not making sense.<br /> <br /> By the way, the cyber-mages nuking a country and then killing a vampire with a laser from space isn't in any measure less of a problem, quite the contrary. It is so huge that the books currently still refuse to mention it because no one knows what to do with that mess.<br /> <br /> Also, neither of those is Tuesday. They are purposefully written as especially big situations. The difference is that despite all the problems, one of them actually intended to explore consequences and throw the setting into its final nights, when the Masquerade could very well be torn apart as a result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468001#post1468001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the issue is that a lot of people keep trying to make this a monolithic organization when it is explictly not.</div> </div> </div> </div>This person is you.<br /> <br /> My problem with how the Vienna Incident was written is precisely that it would pretty much take a monolithic organization to pull it out the way it was written.<br /> <br /> You're saying repeatedly that it makes sense because they have the power, resources, intelligence and influence of a monolithic organization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T10:00:41-08:00","id":1468018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468007#post1468007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want a hypercompetent/hyperpowerful SI. But Vienna? Only makes sense with a hypercompetent SI. But then the setting, doesn't want a hypercompetent SI. Do you see the problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't. I think that you can have tremendous influence over the government in an area and not be hypercompetent in others. I don't think governments work the way you do. I don't think the way you're describing the events in Vienna approach the way canon does. I think that if the events happened and someone blew up a castle of vampires that it would be a few week of news and then be forgotten, especially since no one died in it that would be listed as an actual citizen of the world. Especially in the World of Darkness where both the Camarilla and SI would both be working to conceal the truth.<br /> <br /> I suppose we're not going to find any common ground.<br /> <br /> Thank you for discussing the issue with me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T10:17:40-08:00","id":1468020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468018#post1468018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I don't. I think that you can have tremendous influence over the government in an area and not be hypercompetent in others. I don't think governments work the way you do. I don't think the way you're describing the events in Vienna approach the way canon does. I think that if the events happened and someone blew up a castle of vampires that it would be a few week of news and then be forgotten, especially since no one died in it that would be listed as an actual citizen of the world. Especially in the World of Darkness where both the Camarilla and SI would both be working to conceal the truth.<br /> <br /> I suppose we're not going to find any common ground.<br /> <br /> Thank you for discussing the issue with me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Camarilla at the time was taking massive structural damage such that it was losing whole cities. The SI concealing the truth of an action like this would on simple logic require it to be a globally powerful monolith. You have no idea how I think governments work considering what I'm talking about is something I have repeatedly said not even real world governments have shown capacity for as far as being able to act like the clandestine global monolith something like Vienna and its nigh perfect coverup would entail, and I'm not sure why you keep ignoring that, it feels like you don't want to question or respond to my actual posts so much as what you want my posts to be in order to fit your responses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that if the events happened and someone blew up a castle of vampires that it would be a few week of news and then be forgotten, especially since no one died in it that would be listed as an actual citizen of the world. </div> </div> </div>You are making an extremely reductionist argument to treat &quot;a multinational military operation using advanced tech, staged an attack in a European city using that tech in a particularly notable way, then so successfully covered up that there were zero problems, even from the nature of its cover story&quot; as equivalent to &quot;someone blew up a castle full of vampires.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's pretty telling that almost no one trying to argue Vienna makes sense actually addresses these points instead of just trying to entirely blow past them.<br /> <br /> In that sense no, I doubt you will find common ground with anyone who has expressed these problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-16-2021, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T10:42:26-08:00","id":1468022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1467900#post1467900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK, everyone seemed to get along just fine with the fact that nobody noticed Pentex had gone Raccoon City with a small town, the sewers of New York hosted the Tzimisce Antediluvian, or that Ebola was a Tzimisce Methuselah, yet now we are shocked by the Second Inquisition telling everyone &amp;quot;Yes, Al Quaeda used a drone to blow up a building&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Perhaps we should be more lenient with our fantasy worlds, they are not academic works of alternate history. \ud83d\ude01 It was over the top? Yes. It was probably poor writing? Yes. Has it happened before in real life? No. Has it happened in Jason Bourne's, Jack Ryan's and similar books? A lot of times, probably. <br /> <br /> I think we should accept than WOD is closer to Jason Bourne than to RL geopolitics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are very poor comparisons.<br /> <br /> 1) Werewolf is not Vampire and as funny as it is as a satire oc caputalism/hyper-consummerism Pentex is cartoonish.<br /> <br /> 2) Comparing a small rural town to a capital city of a central European country is weak.<br /> <br /> 3) Do any mortals know Demdemeh is Ebola?<br /> <br /> WoD has a poor track record when it comes to using bombs. Absimilliard nuking Arikiel, Technocracy nuking Ravnos, Xerxes bombing Enoch. And now this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T11:49:18-08:00","id":1468032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468022#post1468022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WoD has a poor track record when it comes to using bombs. Absimilliard nuking Arikiel, Technocracy nuking Ravnos, Xerxes bombing Enoch. And now this.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>You were told not to post in this thread again<br /> <br /> Take a one day ban.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-16-2021, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T12:15:54-08:00","id":1468035,"title":"","content":"Why is the Vienna Attack being overstated so much? There is very little information on it. We don't even know where on Vienna the Prime Chantry was.<br /> <br /> For all we know, the Chantry could have been a seemingly abandoned building was on the outskirts of town. A few people dying on a terrorist attack in Austria would have been notable, but nothing that uncommon for Europe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T12:27:14-08:00","id":1468036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468035#post1468035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the Vienna Attack being overstated so much? There is very little information on it. We don't even know where on Vienna the Prime Chantry was.<br /> <br /> For all we know, the Chantry could have been a seemingly abandoned building was on the outskirts of town. A few people dying on a terrorist attack in Austria would have been notable, but nothing that uncommon for Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We know that it was an advanced military operation to the point of involving military drone strikes, that occurred within a major European city. And when even the people advocating for it to make sense say things like &quot;well they were probably able to get permission from NATO for an operation within a NATO country&quot; we definitely know there's a level of acknowledgement of how high level an operation that would have to be, just to happen, from even the people trying to defend this.<br /> <br /> The problem of &quot;a few people dying in a terrorist attack in Austria&quot; is that such is the cover story being used to cover up a sequence of events that for including &quot;military drone strikes in Vienna&quot; would require a level of influence, control and integration on an international scale that it creates the &quot;then the SI is ludicrously powerful and competent&quot; issue.<br /> <br /> The problem is the continuing efforts to skip over &quot;military drone strikes in Europe within a major city&quot; with &quot;well the cover story means there was no problem&quot; for how powerful the SI would have to be for &quot;well the cover story means there was no problem.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T12:27:15-08:00","id":1468037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468035#post1468035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the Vienna Attack being overstated so much? There is very little information on it. We don't even know where on Vienna the Prime Chantry was.<br /> <br /> For all we know, the Chantry could have been a seemingly abandoned building was on the outskirts of town. A few people dying on a terrorist attack in Austria would have been notable, but nothing that uncommon for Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly, it is stated the chantry teleported like Count Duckula's castle in a pattern around Vienna. At least as of V20.<br /> <br /> Magic prevented the population from noticing its existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know that it was an advanced military operation to the point of involving military drone strikes, that occurred within a major European city. And when even the people advocating for it to make sense say things like &quot;well they were able to get permission from NATO for an operation within a NATO country&quot; we definitely know there's a level of acknowledgement of how high level an operation that would have to be, just to happen.<br /> <br /> The problem of &quot;a few people dying in a terrorist attack in Austria&quot; is that such is the cover story being used to cover up a sequence of events that for including &quot;military drone strikes in Vienna&quot; would require a level of influence, control and integration on an international scale that it creates the &quot;then the SI is ludicrously powerful and competent&quot; issue.<br /> <br /> The problem is the continuing efforts to skip over &quot;military drone strikes in Europe within a major city&quot; with &quot;well the cover story means there was no problem&quot; for how powerful the SI would have to be for &quot;well the cover story means there was no problem.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which gets back to the point that &quot;military drone strike&quot; only requires you to be able to corrupt the people who would investigate it. It was a Al-Qaeda bombing that destroyed a abandoned ruin and killed no one and only known to be a drone strike by the people who are involved with the Second Inquisition. You have yet to name the people who would object to it and how they know of it.<br /> <br /> And why.<br /> <br /> Who is the group that requires the most powerful organization in the world to fool and why do they know? Please walk me through this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-16-2021, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T12:58:04-08:00","id":1468043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468037#post1468037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weirdly, it is stated the chantry teleported like Count Duckula's castle in a pattern around Vienna. At least as of V20.<br /> <br /> Magic prevented the population from noticing its existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which gets back to the point that &quot;military drone strike&quot; only requires you to be able to corrupt the people who would investigate it. It was a Al-Qaeda bombing that destroyed a abandoned ruin and killed no one and only known to be a drone strike by the people who are involved with the Second Inquisition. You have yet to name the people who would object to it and how they know of it.<br /> <br /> And why.<br /> <br /> Who is the group that requires the most powerful organization in the world to fool and why do they know? Please walk me through this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything from NATO itself having to either be controlled or gulled to not have any issues with a major military operation going off within the middle of Europe, the satelites and radar that tend to pick up things like missile attacks on the ground either not doing so or being controlled not to do so, the various international intelligence bodies that would similarly need to be compromised or controlled as far as awareness or subsequent looking into things, the Austrian government itself needing to either be suborned or brought along onto an operation comprised of international troops using advanced tech in their territory..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have yet to name the people who would object to it and how they know of it. </div> </div> </div>I've named everything from the CIA to NATO, as examples, in previous posts, several times as things that either need to be compromised or controlled for what happened for this to be possible. That you are now saying this lines up pretty well with my noting you don't seem to want to reply to my posts as reply to what you say my posts are. How would they know of it? Once again, in the modern world we live in, when terrorist attacks occur in the Western world there is in fact a generally considerable effort to investigate them. There is a considerable effort to have technology in play to try and be able to read from things like missile attacks going off, even if only to examine the explosion effects after the fact. Cities, especially major European capitals, have stations and bureaus from a variety of groups as far as international intelligence agencies even for just a very simple &quot;well we should probably look into that violent thing that happened in the place where all our major embassies with an entire nation and operational bureaus are&quot;. A military ordinance attack going off in Vienna blamed on terrorists is going to require all of them going &quot;eh, that was fine.&quot;<br /> <br /> I find it interesting that there are other posts, by monteparnas for instance, going into pretty heavy depth with why these things couldn't be brushed off as easily as you claim, but you only really reply to mine, and in ways that demonstrate you are reading my posts as selectively as you possibly can.<br /> <br /> Even the attempt Manfr made at &quot;well look at these real world attacks&quot;, it was observed that if cover ups did happen there, they in fact failed because information did get out for controversies and ongoing fights involving goverment figures to happen. And that was with the attention the world paid to those things and the technology in play from decades upon decades ago. By 2008? Stuff improves. And the entire strategic paradigm of the world shifted in the meantime.<br /> <br /> I said this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>If the cover story did not address that drone strikes happened, it means the Second Inquisition basically controls... Western intelligence agencies, various governments, the media, and lord knows NATO as far as being able to hide from them that drone strikes happened.</i> </div> </div> </div>I said this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They would be trying to fool the media, NATO, the CIA, a variety of other national intelligence agencies, Western militaries, the governments of those nations. Alternatively, they don't need to fool them, they control all those things, and we're back to &quot;why are vampires still alive if the Second Inquisition is that powerful.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I said this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;People&quot; are not everything from the CIA to NATO as far as what would either need to be already controlled by the SI, or be able to be fooled by the SI. You seem to feel you can ignore the difference of scale here for what th implications, and that's just not how things work. </div> </div> </div>While otherwise noting things like, say, satelites that observe things, chains of command that would be aware of things as far as operational planning using their forces. For instance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Satellites are even purposed to that kind of thing. The idea of non stateless actors acquiring drone strike technology on par with that of developed nations (which is what you would have if they had the technology to straight up end a building in the middle of Europe with one) probably keeps these groupings up at night with dread. This isn't some thing in some airspace somewhere. It's an attack, right on the ground, of a major European city, using major military technology.<br /> <br /> If these things are not thus in on said plot, that crap will be noticed, and then they'll freak. And if these things are instead in on said plot? Well hey, we're right back at &quot;why are vampires still alive if the SI controls that much of the socipolitical organization of the world.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Despite all that, you said this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have yet to name the people who would object to it and how they know of it. </div> </div> </div>How am I able to go forward thinking you're actually trying to discuss what I post at this point, instead of what version of it you decided I posted instead?<br /> <br /> But just to put something else out there, when SOCOM operations happen, a thing that was brought forth as a defense of all this as far as &quot;well SOCOM has influence over NATO&quot; that means there is an entire developed, powerful chain of command aware of them, and thus one that has to be so compromised to miss them.<br /> <br /> I've named all kinds of people/organizations that would need to be brought in on this. If you missed that, I don't know what to tell you. If you think they wouldn't as is find out about this sort of thing, you're right, we're right back at not agreeing how the world works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who is the group that requires the most powerful organization in the world to fool and why do they know? Please walk me through this. </div> </div> </div>It is extremely difficult to take at face value the idea that you want me to answer questions you ask when you are already straight up ignoring the content of things I say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-16-2021, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T14:13:32-08:00","id":1468048,"title":"","content":"Maybe a change in perspective might help here. Let's say that somebody drops a plane on top of a pentagonal building outside the capitol of the USA. What would the reactions be and how would people react to something like that? Would there be repercussions, reaction and conspiracy theories? Would there be fallout in the other states? Would there be reactions and repercussions in global geopolitics over this?<br /> <br /> Look at what happened after Bataclan. France was closed down, military was on the streets, and the people involved were hunted across the breath of Europe. This is not a &quot;oh and it just happened&quot;. It's a huge thing with major repercussions and consequences. Heck, France was under state of emergency for a better part of the year.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T14:54:12-08:00","id":1468051,"title":"","content":"And it is not a matter of victims.<br /> <br /> If there was an airstrike and an invasion force of more than two dozen soldiers then it was a noticeable thing. People won't care because it was an important building or a lot of deaths, people will care because, again:<br /> <br /> <b>Drone strike. Blamed on terrorists. In Vienna.</b><br /> <br /> Not gunman, not suicide bomber, not a guy on a truck and a knife.<br /> <br /> By the way, convincing only the people that would investigate, in this day and age, means <b><u>convincing the internet</u></b>, the people that can pinpoint a flag that could be anywhere in the US (and maybe in another country) in less than 38 hours just watching a live feed of the sky, or use a record of an execution to locate a rebel training camp in Syria.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T15:17:44-08:00","id":1468057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468051#post1468051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it is not a matter of victims.<br /> <br /> If there was an airstrike and an invasion force of more than two dozen soldiers then it was a noticeable thing. People won't care because it was an important building or a lot of deaths, people will care because, again:<br /> <br /> <b>Drone strike. Blamed on terrorists. In Vienna.</b><br /> <br /> Not gunman, not suicide bomber, not a guy on a truck and a knife.<br /> <br /> By the way, convincing only the people that would investigate, in this day and age, means <b><u>convincing the internet</u></b>, the people that can pinpoint a flag that could be anywhere in the US (and maybe in another country) in less than 38 hours just watching a live feed of the sky, or use a record of an execution to locate a rebel training camp in Syria.</div> </div> </div> </div>The internet seems a very strange place to argue as a source of journalistic integrity now since in RL we have things like Q which claim the Democrats of my country are vampires and Satanists.<br /> <br /> Also that 9/11 was an inside job.<br /> <br /> Any claims that it was an Austrian inside job would be very....questionable by the public.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T15:30:01-08:00","id":1468060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468057#post1468057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The internet seems a very strange place to argue as a source of journalistic integrity now since in RL we have things like Q which claim the Democrats of my country are vampires and Satanists.<br /> <br /> Also that 9/11 was an inside job.<br /> <br /> Any claims that it was an Austrian inside job would be very....questionable by the public.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You seem to again be reading a post and responding to something in it that isn't there. It's not the point of journalistic integrity. It's the point of things being noticed and then put forward. And since we're talking about the whole flipping between &quot;the SI wouldn't have needed to co opt any of these organizations&quot; to &quot;no, wait, they totally did&quot; and back and forth and back and forth, if something is flying around the internet of a military drone strike in Vienna, we're right back to the sweeping pile of international groups that would proceed to want to make sure that no, military a drone strike did not happen in Vienna because of the sheer implications of if it did.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you can roll with that they wouldn't want to make sure of that, because the SI has totally co opted all those groups, in which case we're right back to the SI would logically by some hypercompetent global monolith.<br /> <br /> Or, and hear me out, the Vienna attack was a bad piece of writing that fits poorly into what you feel the intended setting is, and attempting to claim otherwise has resulted in a lot of pages now of back and forth contradictions, disregarding the content of posts, and otherwise ignoring notions of context, scale and scope and implication as far as things like, y'know, the use of advanced military hardware in a staged attack in a European capital in 2008.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-16-2021, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T15:31:01-08:00","id":1468061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468057#post1468057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The internet seems a very strange place to argue as a source of journalistic integrity now since in RL we have things like Q which claim the Democrats of my country are vampires and Satanists.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're missing is that the point isn't to uncover the truth, it is to have repercussions.<br /> <br /> If they blame the attack on a terrorist bombing, and some people in the internet have info that there was a drone in the area, people will reach conclusions. And will act on these conclusions.<br /> <br /> <b>That</b> is what I see lacking. If those conclusions are near the truth is immaterial to their repercussions, that can be anything from a new batch of defense laws, protests, international accusations being thrown around, political use of anything that comes up.<br /> <br /> You're too focused on thinking that consequence means finding the truth. No. Consequence means consequence. An inquiry in the US senate about a unit going AWOL hours before a US drone is seen in Austrian airspace, and then a bomb goes off and the drone comes missing some ordnance. This inquiry may settle for a false narrative and yet increase security measures against theft of armament, a lot of people is promoted, a lot go to jail, and the avenue used to get the equipment is closed. This is an example of a consequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T15:32:44-08:00","id":1468062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468051#post1468051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it is not a matter of victims.<br /> <br /> If there was an airstrike and an invasion force of more than two dozen soldiers then it was a noticeable thing. People won't care because it was an important building or a lot of deaths, people will care because, again:<br /> <br /> <b>Drone strike. Blamed on terrorists. In Vienna.</b><br /> <br /> Not gunman, not suicide bomber, not a guy on a truck and a knife.<br /> <br /> By the way, convincing only the people that would investigate, in this day and age, means <b><u>convincing the internet</u></b>, the people that can pinpoint a flag that could be anywhere in the US (and maybe in another country) in less than 38 hours just watching a live feed of the sky, or use a record of an execution to locate a rebel training camp in Syria.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a handful lines in the entirety of V5 talking about how the Chantry got destroyed. As I said before, we don't know who witnessed the attack, what exactly the public saw, what remained afterward, how it was covered up (besides that it was blamed on terrorists). It could very well have been an old building that collapsed when a bomb accidentally went off in a failed terrorist attack. Maybe a coalition of Ur-Shulgi, Saulot, Tzimisce and Carna all pulled strings to make sure the attack happened<br /> <br /> Regardless, there is barely any information, you can't get too deep into it without inevitably making assumption to suit one's viewpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T15:40:15-08:00","id":1468064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468062#post1468062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are a handful lines in the entirety of V5 talking about how the Chantry got destroyed. As I said before, we don't know who witnessed the attack, what exactly the public saw, what remained afterward, how it was covered up (besides that it was blamed on terrorists). It could very well have been an old building that collapsed when a bomb accidentally went off in a failed terrorist attack. Maybe a coalition of Ur-Shulgi, Saulot, Tzimisce and Carna all pulled strings to make sure the attack happened<br /> <br /> Regardless, there is barely any information, you can't get too deep into it without inevitably making assumption to suit one's viewpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's enough information to make references to SOCOM, and military drone strikes. That's enough information to then invoke the problem of every organization and piece of technology possessed by a variety of organizations that are intended to look out for things like missile attacks in European capitals. That's enough information to invoke the problem of the chain of command required to authorize things like military action in a NATO country, let alone military action involving, y'know, drone strikes in a European capital. That's enough information to invoke the problem of that we've had an entire global security strategic shift in the last couple decades that stuff like &quot;terrorist attack in European capital city where things blew up&quot; gets investigated with international attention, regardless of its nature. That's enough information to invoke the problem of &quot;given how surveillance and the world works by 2008, the idea of a military drone strike in Vienna not getting noticed even just online is thin.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe a coalition of Ur-Shulgi, Saulot, Tzimisce and Carna all pulled strings to make sure the attack happened </div> </div> </div>You can totally make up whatever offscreen thing you want to be headcanon to say this is in fact not a problem, you bet. But unless the SI book ever actually clarifies beyond what is noted, all those problems remain.<br /> <br /> The best you seem capable of saying is &quot;well it wasn't a problem because it wasn't a problem&quot;. That's what a tautology fallacy is, and again, bad writing.<br /> <br /> Or: &quot;It wasn't a problem because the reader can make up for themselves why it wasn't a problem&quot; is pretty deeply lazy writing.<br /> <br /> Or: If you want to try &quot;well the SI was clearly then powerful, influential and competent enough to make all above that stuff not be a problem&quot; instead then we're right back to, as always, how are vampires existing in their current state, at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-16-2021, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T16:48:00-08:00","id":1468073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468064#post1468064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's enough information to make references to SOCOM, and military drone strikes. That's enough information to then invoke the problem of every organization and piece of technology possessed by a variety of organizations that are intended to look out for things like missile attacks in European capitals. That's enough information to invoke the problem of the chain of command required to authorize things like military action in a NATO country, let alone military action involving, y'know, drone strikes in a European capital. That's enough information to invoke the problem of that we've had an entire global security strategic shift in the last couple decades that stuff like &quot;terrorist attack in European capital city where things blew up&quot; gets investigated with international attention, regardless of its nature. That's enough information to invoke the problem of &quot;given how surveillance and the world works by 2008, the idea of a military drone strike in Vienna not getting noticed even just online is thin.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The SI's members in different Governments, who used their influence in order to do it without proper CoC. Afterwards the higher-up pulled strings to cover up, blamed middle management when pressed by the rest of the command chain. SI lost influence but the Military covered up in order to save face and not expose that they allowed it to happen. Whatever explanation one finds, this all leads to the point bellow:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468064#post1468064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can totally make up whatever offscreen thing you want to be headcanon to say this is in fact not a problem, you bet. But unless the SI book ever actually clarifies beyond what is noted, all those problems remain.</div> </div> </div> </div>The attack is barely detailed in the books, you obviously need to make headcanon to explain it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468064#post1468064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best you seem capable of saying is &quot;well it wasn't a problem because it wasn't a problem&quot;. That's what a tautology fallacy is, and again, bad writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a real need to start personal attacks? Maybe you should take a break.<br /> <br /> It isn't problem because it is described in a vague enough way to provide for a number of plausible explanations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468064#post1468064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or: &quot;It wasn't a problem because the reader can make up for themselves why it wasn't a problem&quot; is pretty deeply lazy writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's vague so the ST can make it up for themselves if they wish to include it. It's not meant to be &quot;Vienna: What happened&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468064#post1468064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or: If you want to try &quot;well the SI was clearly then powerful, influential and competent enough to make all above that stuff not be a problem&quot; instead then we're right back to, as always, how are vampires existing in their current state, at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Power comes and goes, it's been years since the Vienna and London, Kindred have adapted, SI lost influence. Writers wanted to break the status-quo but keep the option for old styles of political intrigue with little hunter involvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T16:48:28-08:00","id":1468074,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I think we should move on. Thanks for everyone's participation in the Vienna subject.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T16:58:16-08:00","id":1468076,"title":"","content":"I just don't understand why it is that, just because the SI is capable of blowing up a building in Vienna and getting it written off as a terrorist attack, this would logically mean that they must have the resources and manpower to wipe out all vampires everywhere. I'm not following the logic where just because the one happened means that the other must have happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T17:08:54-08:00","id":1468078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465534-preview-of-the-si-book?p=1468076#post1468076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't understand why it is that, just because the SI is capable of blowing up a building in Vienna and getting it written off as a terrorist attack, this would logically mean that they must have the resources and manpower to wipe out all vampires everywhere. I'm not following the logic where just because the one happened means that the other must have happened.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">The subject has been asked to move on. The thread will be closed if it is mentioned again.</span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www